Z||000000||AL||09-01-99||07:24 PM||||i just bought an 86 gt, when i turn it on, the fan is working constantly. it doesn't turn off, what can i do for this problem?,also, is ther a way to tell by looking at car that the recalls have been done? i try calling pontiac but i get home from work to late so they are closed.<br>
Z||000001||88 Fiero||09-01-99||07:27 PM||||one way of checking is the rubber tube that connects to your car's throttle body and to the air filter housing should be one piece and not 2 pieces. If it's 2 pieces then you need it to bring it in for the recall. But assuming your car is an '86 model recall should have been done....
Z||000002||AL||09-01-99||08:14 PM||||well it has two hoses so i guess it <br>wasn't done(recall)so what do i do now? <br>should i take the car to the <br>dealer?fiero88
Z||000003||88 Fiero||09-01-99||08:22 PM||||If the 2 large hoses that your talking about is where the air goes through from the air filter and the throttle body then you need to call pontiac dealer and set-up for a recall job....
Z||000004||AL||09-01-99||08:24 PM||||i will thanks, fiero88. what about the fan running all the time? do you know why? is this normal?
Z||000005||batboy||09-02-99||04:31 AM||||If your cooling fan runs for more than a few seconds after you shut the engine off, something is wrong. Does run all night if you leave it parked? If so, there might be a problem with the temperature switch, I'd start there.
Z||000006||AL||09-02-99||06:44 PM||||no actually it stays on as soon as i start the car, and it doesn't go off. my t'a only goes on when it is hot, but on the fiero it doesn't stop.
Z||000007||AL||09-02-99||06:46 PM||||no actually it stays on as soon as i <br>start the car, and it doesn't go off. my <br>t'a only goes on when it is hot, but on <br>the fiero it doesn't stop.until i turn the car off
Z||000008||batboy||09-02-99||07:30 PM||||Normally on Fieros, the cooling fan comes on at 235 degrees or whenever you turn on the air conditioner. Some people have wired the fan directly so that it comes on all the time when the key is on. This might be what is going on with your car.
Z||000009||AL||09-02-99||07:53 PM||||so is that bad or what? i kinda like it, to turn on, when it get's hot and shut off when it gets back to normal temp.
Z||000010||batboy||09-02-99||08:00 PM||||Obviously, it will put more wear and tear on your cooling fan motor, but other than that, it shouldn't be bad for the car. In some cases, it could be good (like stop and go driving on a hot day). If most of your driving is on the highway, then having your fan run constantly is not really helping much at all.
